   {
    "id": "p_00006",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The mutex object referenced by [I5]mutex[/I5] shall be locked by a call to [I6]pthread_mutex_lock[/I6]() that returns zero or\n[EOWNERDEAD]. If the mutex is already locked by another thread, the calling thread shall block until the mutex becomes available.\nThis operation shall return with the mutex object referenced by [I7]mutex[/I7] in the locked state with the calling thread as its\nowner. If a thread attempts to relock a mutex that it has already locked, [I8]pthread_mutex_lock[/I8]() shall behave as described in\nthe [B9]Relock[/B9] column of the following table. If a thread attempts to unlock a mutex that it has not locked or a mutex which is\nunlocked, [I10]pthread_mutex_unlock[/I10]() shall behave as described in the [B11]Unlock When Not Owner[/B11] column of the following\ntable.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I5": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
