   {
    "id": "dd_00032",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     5,
     5
    ],
    "text": "If the mutex type is PTHREAD_MUTEX_DEFAULT, the behavior of [I15]pthread_mutex_lock[/I15]() may correspond to one of the three\nother standard mutex types as described in the table above. If it does not correspond to one of those three, the behavior is\nundefined for the cases marked †.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I15": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00033",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     7
    ],
    "text": "Where the table indicates recursive behavior, the mutex shall maintain the concept of a lock count. When a thread\nsuccessfully acquires a mutex for the first time, the lock count shall be set to one. Every time a thread relocks this mutex, the\nlock count shall be incremented by one. Each time the thread unlocks the mutex, the lock count shall be decremented by one. When\nthe lock count reaches zero, the mutex shall become available for other threads to acquire.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00034",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I16]pthread_mutex_trylock[/I16]() function shall be equivalent to [I17]pthread_mutex_lock[/I17](), except that if the\nmutex object referenced by [I18]mutex[/I18] is currently locked (by any thread, including the current thread), the call shall return\nimmediately. If the mutex type is PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE and the mutex is currently owned by the calling thread, the mutex lock\ncount shall be incremented by one and the [I19]pthread_mutex_trylock[/I19]() function shall immediately return success.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I16": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I17": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I18": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I19": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00035",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     11
    ],
    "text": "The [I20]pthread_mutex_unlock[/I20]() function shall release the mutex object referenced by [I21]mutex[/I21]. The manner in\nwhich a mutex is released is dependent upon the mutex's type attribute. If there are threads blocked on the mutex object referenced\nby [I22]mutex[/I22] when [I23]pthread_mutex_unlock[/I23]() is called, resulting in the mutex becoming available, the scheduling policy\nshall determine which thread shall acquire the mutex.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I20": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I21": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I22": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I23": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00036",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     13
    ],
    "text": "(In the case of PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE mutexes, the mutex shall become available when the count reaches zero and\nthe calling thread no longer has any locks on this mutex.)",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00037",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     15
    ],
    "text": "If a signal is delivered to a thread waiting for a mutex, upon return from the signal handler the thread shall\nresume waiting for the mutex as if it was not interrupted.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00038",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     17
    ],
    "text": "If [I24]mutex[/I24] is a robust mutex and the process containing the owning thread terminated while holding the mutex\nlock, a call to [I25]pthread_mutex_lock[/I25]() shall return the error value [EOWNERDEAD]. If [I26]mutex[/I26] is a robust mutex and the\nowning thread terminated while holding the mutex lock, a call to [I27]pthread_mutex_lock[/I27]() may return the error value\n[EOWNERDEAD] even if the process in which the owning thread resides has not terminated. In these cases, the mutex shall be locked\nby the calling thread but the state it protects is marked as inconsistent. The application should ensure that the state is made\nconsistent for reuse and when that is complete call [A28][I29]pthread_mutex_consistent[/I29]()[/A28]. If the application is unable to recover the\nstate, it should unlock the mutex without a prior call to [A30][I31]pthread_mutex_consistent[/I31]()[/A30], after which the mutex is marked permanently\nunusable.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I24": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I25": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I26": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I27": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A28": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/pthread_mutex_consistent.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I29": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A30": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/pthread_mutex_consistent.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I31": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00039",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     21,
     19
    ],
    "text": "If [I32]mutex[/I32] does not refer to an initialized mutex object, the behavior of [I33]pthread_mutex_lock[/I33](),\n[I34]pthread_mutex_trylock[/I34](), and [I35]pthread_mutex_unlock[/I35]() is undefined.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I32": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I33": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I34": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I35": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00040",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     23
    ],
    "text": "[A36][/A36]RETURN VALUE",
    "placeholders": {
