     13
    ],
    "text": "[S44][[A45]RPP|TPP[/A45]][/S44] [IMG46] The [I47]mutex[/I47] was created with the protocol attribute having the value PTHREAD_PRIO_PROTECT and the calling thread's\npriority is higher than the mutex's current priority ceiling. [IMG48]",
    "placeholders": {
     "S44": {
      "open": "<sup>",
      "close": "</sup>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A45": {
      "open": "<a href=\"javascript:open_code(&#x27;RPP&#x27;)\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG46": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-start.gif\" alt=\"[Option Start]\" border=\"0\">"
     },
     "I47": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "IMG48": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<img src=\"../images/opt-end.gif\" alt=\"[Option End]\" border=\"0\">"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00050",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     15
    ],
    "text": "[ENOTRECOVERABLE]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00051",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     17
    ],
    "text": "The state protected by the mutex is not recoverable.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00052",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     19
    ],
    "text": "[EOWNERDEAD]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00053",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     3,
     21
    ],
    "text": "The mutex is a robust mutex and the process containing the previous owning thread terminated while holding the mutex lock. The\nmutex lock shall be acquired by the calling thread and it is up to the new owner to make the state consistent.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00054",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I49]pthread_mutex_lock[/I49]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I49": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00055",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     7,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EDEADLK]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00056",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     7,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The mutex type is PTHREAD_MUTEX_ERRORCHECK and the current thread already owns the mutex.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00057",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     9
    ],
    "text": "The [I50]pthread_mutex_trylock[/I50]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I50": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00058",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     11,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EBUSY]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00059",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     11,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I51]mutex[/I51] could not be acquired because it was already locked.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I51": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00060",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     13
    ],
    "text": "The [I52]pthread_mutex_unlock[/I52]() function shall fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I52": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00061",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     15,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EPERM]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00062",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     15,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The mutex type is PTHREAD_MUTEX_ERRORCHECK or PTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE, or the mutex is a robust mutex, and the current thread\ndoes not own the mutex.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00063",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     19
    ],
    "text": "The [I53]pthread_mutex_lock[/I53]() and [I54]pthread_mutex_trylock[/I54]() functions may fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I53": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I54": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00064",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     21,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EOWNERDEAD]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00065",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     21,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The mutex is a robust mutex and the previous owning thread terminated while holding the mutex lock. The mutex lock shall be\nacquired by the calling thread and it is up to the new owner to make the state consistent.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00066",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     23
    ],
    "text": "The [I55]pthread_mutex_lock[/I55]() function may fail if:",
    "placeholders": {
     "I55": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dt_00067",
    "type": "dt",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     25,
     3
    ],
    "text": "[EDEADLK]",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "dd_00068",
    "type": "dd",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     25,
     5
    ],
    "text": "A deadlock condition was detected.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00069",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     29,
     27
    ],
    "text": "These functions shall not return an error code of [EINTR].",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00070",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     35
    ],
    "text": "[A56][/A56]EXAMPLES",
    "placeholders": {
     "A56": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_442_06\" id=\"tag_17_442_06\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00071",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     37,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00072",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     39
    ],
    "text": "[A57][/A57]APPLICATION USAGE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A57": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_442_07\" id=\"tag_17_442_07\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00073",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     41,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Applications that have assumed that non-zero return values are errors will need updating for use with robust mutexes, since a\nvalid return for a thread acquiring a mutex which is protecting a currently inconsistent state is [EOWNERDEAD]. Applications that\ndo not check the error returns, due to ruling out the possibility of such errors arising, should not use robust mutexes. If an\napplication is supposed to work with normal and robust mutexes it should check all return values for error conditions and if\nnecessary take appropriate action.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00074",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     43
    ],
    "text": "[A58][/A58]RATIONALE",
    "placeholders": {
     "A58": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_442_08\" id=\"tag_17_442_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00075",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     1
    ],
    "text": "Mutex objects are intended to serve as a low-level primitive from which other thread synchronization functions can be built. As\nsuch, the implementation of mutexes should be as efficient as possible, and this has ramifications on the features available at the\ninterface.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00076",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The mutex functions and the particular default settings of the mutex attributes have been motivated by the desire\nto not preclude fast, inlined implementations of mutex locking and unlocking.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00077",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     5
    ],
    "text": "Since most attributes only need to be checked when a thread is going to be blocked, the use of attributes does not\nslow the (common) mutex-locking case.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00078",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     7
    ],
    "text": "Likewise, while being able to extract the thread ID of the owner of a mutex might be desirable, it would require\nstoring the current thread ID when each mutex is locked, and this could incur unacceptable levels of overhead. Similar arguments\napply to a [I59]mutex_tryunlock[/I59] operation.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I59": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00079",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     9
    ],
    "text": "For further rationale on the extended mutex types, see XRAT [A60][I61]Threads Extensions[/I61][/A60].",
    "placeholders": {
     "A60": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../xrat/V4_xsh_chap01.html#tag_22_02_09_08\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I61": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00080",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     45,
     11
    ],
    "text": "If an implementation detects that the value specified by the [I62]mutex[/I62] argument does not refer to an initialized\nmutex object, it is recommended that the function should fail and report an [EINVAL] error.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I62": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00081",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     47
    ],
    "text": "[A63][/A63]FUTURE DIRECTIONS",
    "placeholders": {
     "A63": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_442_09\" id=\"tag_17_442_09\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00082",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     49,
     1
    ],
    "text": "None.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00083",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     51
    ],
    "text": "[A64][/A64]SEE ALSO",
    "placeholders": {
     "A64": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_442_10\" id=\"tag_17_442_10\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
