   },
   {
    "id": "p_00085",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     53,
     3
    ],
    "text": "XBD [A73][I74]4.15.2 Memory Synchronization[/I74][/A73], [A75][I76]&lt;pthread.h&gt;[/I76][/A75]",
    "placeholders": {
     "A73": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/V1_chap04.html#tag_04_15_02\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I74": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "A75": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../basedefs/pthread.h.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I76": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00086",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     55
    ],
    "text": "[A77][/A77]CHANGE HISTORY",
    "placeholders": {
     "A77": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_442_11\" id=\"tag_17_442_11\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00087",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     57,
     1
    ],
    "text": "First released in Issue 5. Included for alignment with the POSIX Threads Extension.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00088",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     59
    ],
    "text": "[A78][/A78]Issue 6",
    "placeholders": {
     "A78": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_442_12\" id=\"tag_17_442_12\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00089",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The [I79]pthread_mutex_lock[/I79](), [I80]pthread_mutex_trylock[/I80](), and [I81]pthread_mutex_unlock[/I81]() functions are marked as part\nof the Threads option.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I79": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I80": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I81": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00090",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     3
    ],
    "text": "The following new requirements on POSIX implementations derive from alignment with the Single UNIX\nSpecification:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "li_00091",
    "type": "li",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     5,
     1
    ],
    "text": "The behavior when attempting to relock a mutex is defined.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00092",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The [A82][I83]pthread_mutex_timedlock[/I83]()[/A82] function is added to\nthe SEE ALSO section for alignment with IEEE&nbsp;Std&nbsp;1003.1d-1999.",
    "placeholders": {
     "A82": {
      "open": "<a href=\"../functions/pthread_mutex_timedlock.html\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I83": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00093",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     61,
     9
    ],
    "text": "IEEE&nbsp;Std&nbsp;1003.1-2001/Cor&nbsp;2-2004, item XSH/TC2/D6/98 is applied, updating the ERRORS section so that\nthe [EDEADLK] error includes detection of a deadlock condition. The RATIONALE section is also reworded to take into account\nnon-XSI-conformant systems.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "h4_00094",
    "type": "h4",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     63
    ],
    "text": "[A84][/A84]Issue 7",
    "placeholders": {
     "A84": {
      "open": "<a name=\"tag_17_442_13\" id=\"tag_17_442_13\">",
      "close": "</a>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00095",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     1
    ],
    "text": "SD5-XSH-ERN-43 is applied, marking the &quot;shall fail&quot; case of the [EINVAL] error as dependent on the Thread Priority Protection\noption.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00096",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     3
    ],
    "text": "Changes are made from The Open Group Technical Standard, 2006, Extended API Set Part 3.",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00097",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     5
    ],
    "text": "The [I85]pthread_mutex_lock[/I85](), [I86]pthread_mutex_trylock[/I86](), and [I87]pthread_mutex_unlock[/I87]() functions are\nmoved from the Threads option to the Base.",
    "placeholders": {
     "I85": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I86": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     },
     "I87": {
      "open": "<i>",
      "close": "</i>",
      "translate": true
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00098",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     7
    ],
    "text": "The following extended mutex types are moved from the XSI option to the Base:",
    "placeholders": {},
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "blockquote_00099",
    "type": "blockquote",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     9
    ],
    "text": "[PRE88]",
    "placeholders": {
     "PRE88": {
      "open": "",
      "close": "",
      "translate": false,
      "raw": "<pre>\nPTHREAD_MUTEX_NORMAL\nPTHREAD_MUTEX_ERRORCHECK\nPTHREAD_MUTEX_RECURSIVE\nPTHREAD_MUTEX_DEFAULT\n</pre>"
     }
    },
    "context": null
   },
   {
    "id": "p_00100",
    "type": "p",
    "path": [
     2,
     3,
     2,
     65,
     11
    ],
    "text": "The DESCRIPTION is updated to clarify the behavior when [I89]mutex[/I89] does not refer to an initialized mutex.",
